  "configuration_id": "config_011",
  "reason": "The completed experiments show a strong RNA-only direction: multiprofile with scvi_n200 reaches about 0.65 validation accuracy, while singleprofile RNA is much weaker and PCA is inferior to scvi. However, there is no evidence yet for the image modality, so the key uncertainty is whether image features contain useful signal before investing in multimodal fusion. config_011 tests image-only performance under multiprofile with a standard ResNet50 encoder and simple avgpool aggregation, making it directly comparable to the RNA multiprofile avgpool baseline while avoiding extra confounds from fusion, transformer aggregation, or a larger ViT. This is the best next use of budget because it is a simple, informative exploration of the untested image modality: if image-only is competitive, multimodal extensions become justified; if not, complex multimodal configurations are less attractive."
}

